(1070569, 129478, 22046, '<td valign="top">Love the colors.</td>', 'Love the colors.', '2004-12-20 12:02:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070581, 129477, 7628, '<td valign="top">Well done to catch "plagiarize" in the circle AND have good focus on the rest of the page - it is a fine tribute, a well executed photo, and a nice twist.  Wish the background were white or black and not woodgrain, but as is it works okay and is not particularly distracting. 8</td>', 'Well done to catch "plagiarize" in the circle AND have good focus on the rest of the page - it is a fine tribute, a well executed photo, and a nice twist.  Wish the background were white or black and not woodgrain, but as is it works okay and is not particularly distracting. 8', '2004-12-20 12:12:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070584, 128895, 9939, '<td valign="top">I like the way this differs from the original. Nicely done.</td>', 'I like the way this differs from the original. Nicely done.', '2004-12-20 12:17:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070586, 128573, 9939, '<td valign="top">Nice- a faithful recreation with a slight twist. I like it.</td>', 'Nice- a faithful recreation with a slight twist. I like it.', '2004-12-20 12:19:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070602, 129377, 17103, '<td valign="top">Great job!</td>', 'Great job!', '2004-12-20 12:32:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070614, 129056, 17203, '<td valign="top">Too funny (this was my original plan, but I couldn''t find a skeleton). Thanks for finishing it off. Cobwebs would help, as would a dusting of flour or something on the shiny chess board (it looks new). The watch is a nice touch, but down at the elbow most people will miss it. My model thought it was hilarious("I''M DEAD!").</td>', 'Too funny (this was my original plan, but I couldn''t find a skeleton). Thanks for finishing it off. Cobwebs would help, as would a dusting of flour or something on the shiny chess board (it looks new). The watch is a nice touch, but down at the elbow most people will miss it. My model thought it was hilarious("I''M DEAD!").', '2004-12-20 12:36:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070616, 128768, 6999, '<td valign="top">Fabulous. Subversive, silly, appropriate, and plain daft all at once. I wonder if, given the model, you mightn''t have just kept the noise of the sky under more control - I think to have such a silly image (in the best sense) reproduced at the highest quality would be ideal. But great thinking.</td>', 'Fabulous. Subversive, silly, appropriate, and plain daft all at once. I wonder if, given the model, you mightn''t have just kept the noise of the sky under more control - I think to have such a silly image (in the best sense) reproduced at the highest quality would be ideal. But great thinking.', '2004-12-20 12:39:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070620, 128961, 6999, '<td valign="top">Myy first thought is ''which shot is this based on?'' There have been so many shots of refractions through glass that it''s difficult to retain them all in mind, I find. The bobbly bits down the edge ring a bell, vaguely, I think. Anyhow, good shooting - control of sharpness is i think the key to such a very graphic image, especially with such hard edges between black and white.</td>', 'Myy first thought is ''which shot is this based on?'' There have been so many shots of refractions through glass that it''s difficult to retain them all in mind, I find. The bobbly bits down the edge ring a bell, vaguely, I think. Anyhow, good shooting - control of sharpness is i think the key to such a very graphic image, especially with such hard edges between black and white.', '2004-12-20 12:42:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070621, 128862, 17203, '<td valign="top">Great minds think alike!  I was planning all week to shoot the exact same thing (with the advantage of the orginal props), but I didn''t have time to borrow my neighbor''s cat. Thanks for saving me the trouble. The focus on the cat is a little soft, and some color in the fish bowl would be nice, but the tongue is priceless. 9</td>', 'Great minds think alike!  I was planning all week to shoot the exact same thing (with the advantage of the orginal props), but I didn''t have time to borrow my neighbor''s cat. Thanks for saving me the trouble. The focus on the cat is a little soft, and some color in the fish bowl would be nice, but the tongue is priceless. 9', '2004-12-20 12:43:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070625, 128849, 6999, '<td valign="top">Either the most enormous luck, or the most enormous patience :-) Have you used a sharpening brush around the crest, and the eyes/beak area? The way that little grainy patches have emerged is a pity. For the same impact you''d need more snowflakes passing - but that really is taking the copying idea too far - but my point is that ''bracing aginst the snow storm'' isn''t communicated here as well as in the original. Hope that doesn''t sound harsh judgement, but you have set yourself a very hard task here.</td>', 'Either the most enormous luck, or the most enormous patience :-) Have you used a sharpening brush around the crest, and the eyes/beak area? The way that little grainy patches have emerged is a pity. For the same impact you''d need more snowflakes passing - but that really is taking the copying idea too far - but my point is that ''bracing aginst the snow storm'' isn''t communicated here as well as in the original. Hope that doesn''t sound harsh judgement, but you have set yourself a very hard task here.', '2004-12-20 12:48:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070627, 129156, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''m no fan of pet shots particularly, but this, given the challenge and your chosen source ... I have no idea what to think. I think I like it - both the shot itself, which has the mournful put-upon-ness of a pet when they''re being messed about with, and a nicely subversive realtionship to the original and all it''s many ''close companion pieces''</td>', 'I''m no fan of pet shots particularly, but this, given the challenge and your chosen source ... I have no idea what to think. I think I like it - both the shot itself, which has the mournful put-upon-ness of a pet when they''re being messed about with, and a nicely subversive realtionship to the original and all it''s many ''close companion pieces''', '2004-12-20 12:52:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070632, 129474, 17203, '<td valign="top">A clever twist on the original, marred by a few bugs. The white balance is off, resulting in an overall red cast. The DOF is a little too shallow, and the roller should follow the angle of the brushstrokes on the screen. Pity, too, because it''s really a great idea!</td>', 'A clever twist on the original, marred by a few bugs. The white balance is off, resulting in an overall red cast. The DOF is a little too shallow, and the roller should follow the angle of the brushstrokes on the screen. Pity, too, because it''s really a great idea!', '2004-12-20 12:57:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070635, 129014, 6999, '<td valign="top">I beleieve bod used a blue flourescent tube to light his original, and i think this sufferes in comparison mainly because of the blue part of the light. The important thing about that, for me, was the balance of the internal and external light in the shot, and the use of a tube light meant that he was able to get those elongated reflections in the surface of the toaster, which is unfortunately a missing element from this shot: and its remarkable the impact that small a detail makes.</td>', 'I beleieve bod used a blue flourescent tube to light his original, and i think this sufferes in comparison mainly because of the blue part of the light. The important thing about that, for me, was the balance of the internal and external light in the shot, and the use of a tube light meant that he was able to get those elongated reflections in the surface of the toaster, which is unfortunately a missing element from this shot: and its remarkable the impact that small a detail makes.', '2004-12-20 12:58:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070637, 129214, 17203, '<td valign="top">So this is Jackat? A nice, clean combination of the two originals. I would have cloned out some flaws on the left glass, but this should score very well.</td>', 'So this is Jackat? A nice, clean combination of the two originals. I would have cloned out some flaws on the left glass, but this should score very well.', '2004-12-20 13:00:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070640, 129333, 6999, '<td valign="top">Has the effect, but the bloom itself lacks the sheer density of variation in petals that Setz''s shot had. A worthy effort though.</td>', 'Has the effect, but the bloom itself lacks the sheer density of variation in petals that Setz''s shot had. A worthy effort though.', '2004-12-20 13:00:36.000000', NULL, 1),
