(1070773, 129078, 19978, '<td valign="top">Having two photos in one challenge that are nearly identical as rare, and allows for a side-by-side comparison that is unfamiliar to me as a DPC voter. Your Macintosh selection looks a little dull compared to the other, and maybe a little soft on focus, and just doesn''t "pop" out of the monitor. These are not huge issues though, and I probably would never have mentioned them at all if it weren''t for the easy comparision. I give your image a six and will return for further study.</td>', 'Having two photos in one challenge that are nearly identical as rare, and allows for a side-by-side comparison that is unfamiliar to me as a DPC voter. Your Macintosh selection looks a little dull compared to the other, and maybe a little soft on focus, and just doesn''t "pop" out of the monitor. These are not huge issues though, and I probably would never have mentioned them at all if it weren''t for the easy comparision. I give your image a six and will return for further study.', '2004-12-20 14:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1070780, 128890, 19978, '<td valign="top">Having two photos in one challenge that are nearly identical as rare, and allows for a side-by-side comparison that is unfamiliar to me as a DPC voter. Of the two macintosh apple studies, yours is more vibrant in color, sharper in focus, and just seems to spring from the monitor and activate the ''wow'' factor. The apples are shiner and thus the lighting effect is more noticable. Very well done. I give your image a 7.</td>', 'Having two photos in one challenge that are nearly identical as rare, and allows for a side-by-side comparison that is unfamiliar to me as a DPC voter. Of the two macintosh apple studies, yours is more vibrant in color, sharper in focus, and just seems to spring from the monitor and activate the ''wow'' factor. The apples are shiner and thus the lighting effect is more noticable. Very well done. I give your image a 7.', '2004-12-20 14:21:53.000000', NULL, 1),
