(1075786, 129317, 30861, '<td valign="top">working within the limitations of the inevitable distortion from looking up, you''ve chosen to make the bottomost step a true horizontal. Unfortunately there''s now no "defining vertical" here. As a rule, these work better if you have a defining vertical, and the natural choice here would be the vertical between the doors. This would also bring a true horizontal to the topmost step. All this is a cropping/rotation issue. The problem could have been minimized at the time of exposure, with a tripod and some careful alignment.</td>', 'working within the limitations of the inevitable distortion from looking up, you''ve chosen to make the bottomost step a true horizontal. Unfortunately there''s now no "defining vertical" here. As a rule, these work better if you have a defining vertical, and the natural choice here would be the vertical between the doors. This would also bring a true horizontal to the topmost step. All this is a cropping/rotation issue. The problem could have been minimized at the time of exposure, with a tripod and some careful alignment.', '2004-12-23 20:34:40.000000', NULL, 1),
